From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:14:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkisp2: Adapt set_fmt pad op to the
 v4l2_subdev_client_info argument

The 7.4 merge window added a const struct v4l2_subdev_client_info pointer
to the set_fmt, get_selection and set_selection subdev pad operations.
The rkisp2 v3 series was based on v7.2-rc1 and fails to build with
-Wincompatible-pointer-types on the new prototype. Add the argument to
rkisp2_isp_set_fmt(); it is unused, as in rkisp1.

To be squashed into "media: rockchip: rkisp2: Add rkisp2 driver" when the
series is rebased by its author.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-isp.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-isp.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-isp.c
index 0833ffe57..a0c4bc963 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-isp.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-isp.c
@@ -579,6 +579,7 @@ static void rkisp2_isp_set_sink_fmt(struct rkisp2_isp *isp,
 }
 
 static int rkisp2_isp_set_fmt(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
+			      const struct v4l2_subdev_client_info *ci,
 			      struct v4l2_subdev_state *sd_state,
 			      struct v4l2_subdev_format *fmt)
 {
